End to end
==========

A real trixd over HTTP. Nothing is stubbed inside the daemon: requests go through
Hypercorn, the gate, the plugins and the database, to a Luna and a Prometheus.

The pytest suite
----------------

    TRIXD_E2E=local python -m pytest tests/e2e

starts a trixd process here, on free ports, against fakeluna.py: a stand-in for Luna
and Prometheus that checks tokens as Luna does. Needs nothing but the repository, so a
pipeline runs it.

    TRIXD_E2E_URL=http://<controller>:8051 python -m pytest tests/e2e

runs the same suite against a controller, signing in as TRIXD_E2E_USER and
TRIXD_E2E_PASSWORD (trixd and trixd by default). Port 8051 is on the loopback by
default, so run it on the controller or open the port. The cases that need the shared
secret read it from TRIXD_E2E_SECRET, or from luna.ini when they run on the controller.
Every name the suite creates starts with e2e-, and it removes them when it ends.

What it covers, about 1,500 cases, most generated from docs/openapi.json so a new route
or plugin is covered when it is published:

    test_e2e_access.py   every route as every identity on the ladder, a node token, and
                         six kinds of bad token
    test_e2e_inputs.py   odd path values, bodies of the wrong shape, queries out of range:
                         never a 500
    test_e2e_plugins.py  every plugin unplugged and plugged back three times, reloads at
                         once, reserved names, a site plugin dropped in live
    test_e2e_flows.py    a user's role over its life, the audit trail, a queued service
                         action, a node's hardware rules after boot, a rename through Luna
    test_e2e_stress.py   sustained reads and a boot storm; only with -m stress, scaled by
                         TRIXD_STRESS_NODES, TRIXD_STRESS_THREADS and TRIXD_STRESS_SECONDS

The scripts
-----------

    bash tests/e2e/on-the-controller.sh

On the controller itself: it reads the store, checks the rule files on disk, and checks
that a plugin reload leaves the daemon's process running.

    bash tests/e2e/node-rename.sh <node>

On a development controller only: it renames a node at Luna and back.
